From: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 23 Jul 2026 00:05:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: report PPE peer routing failures

The WMI PPE routing command can fail before the host peer map is updated.
That failure is currently silent, including for non-association MLO links
which return immediately after WMI.  Report every failure with enough
context to distinguish vdev, virtual port and enable/disable operations.

ath12k_warn() is device-rate-limited, so repeated recovery failures do not
flood the log.  Keep the existing rollback and host cleanup behavior.

Assisted-by: Codex:GPT-5.6-sol
Signed-off-by: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/ppe.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/ppe.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/ppe.c
@@ -1142,6 +1142,11 @@ void ath12k_ppe_ds_peer_route(struct ath
 	ret = ath12k_wmi_config_peer_ppeds_routing(ar, arsta->addr,
 						   arvif->vdev_id, arvif->ppe_vp,
 					  enable);
+	if (ret)
+		ath12k_warn(ab,
+			    "failed to %s PPE routing for peer %pM vdev %u VP %d: %d\n",
+			    enable ? "enable" : "disable", arsta->addr,
+			    arvif->vdev_id, arvif->ppe_vp, ret);
 	if (!track_peer)
 		return;
 
